  "summary": "All 13 messages in the queue are closed under RBC-RX-05. Every patient who wrote got a reply.\n\n- pt-0026 Gloria Hayes, lisinopril 20 mg (2 messages, handled as 1 request): Oct 5 potassium 6.1 came from a hemolyzed sample, so it doesn't count. The last valid potassium was 4.6 on a BMP from Apr 14. Renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0001) and ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0002).\n- pt-0027 Frank Odum, lisinopril 10 mg: the outside St. Brigid potassium 5.9 (collected Aug 27) was hemolyzed, so it doesn't count. The last valid potassium was 4.5 on a BMP from Jan 20. Renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0006) and ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0007).\n- pt-0027 Frank Odum, amlodipine 5 mg: last completed visit Jan 20. Renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0008).\n- pt-0028 Lena Park, metformin (pharmacy request): **not refilled.** Her Jul 20 eGFR was corrected from 51 to 39 after a lab calibration failure. The plan in your Jul 20 note was based on the old values. I sent you an urgent task to review it (task-t0014, about mr-00287). The current metformin order is still active, not held.\n- pt-0028 Lena Park, lisinopril 10 mg: no BMP in the past 12 months, because the outside BMP was collected Oct 2, 2025. Gave 30 days with no refills (mr-t0012) and ordered a BMP (sr-t0013).\n- pt-0029 Evelyn Brooks, lisinopril 20 mg: **not refilled.** Creatinine rose 38% (0.90 to 1.24) on the BMP 17 days after the dose went up on Sep 21. The protocol treats that the same as a potassium of 5.5 or higher. I sent you an urgent task (task-t0018, about mr-00291). She says she ran out on Oct 20, so this needs a decision soon. Her reply says it is under your review. The current order is still active, not held.\n- pt-0029 Evelyn Brooks, metformin 1000 mg (pharmacy request): eGFR 54. Her last HbA1c was collected Apr 14, just over 6 months ago. Gave 30 days with no refills (mr-t0019) and ordered an HbA1c (sr-t0020).\n- pt-0030 Samuel Price, lisinopril 20 mg: creatinine rose 24% after the dose increase, under the 30% limit, and potassium was 5.2. Renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0024).\n- pt-0030 Samuel Price, metformin 1000 mg (patient and pharmacy, handled as 1 request): eGFR 65 and an outside HbA1c from Aug 19. Renewed once for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0025).\n- pt-0031 Marcus Webb, metformin 500 mg: an Oct 14 eGFR of 39 was marked entered in error (mislabelled sample), so it doesn't count. The valid eGFR is 92 with HbA1c from Sep 28. Renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0032).\n- pt-0031 Marcus Webb, lisinopril 10 mg: his last BMP was collected Oct 20, 2025, just over 12 months ago. Gave 30 days with no refills (mr-t0030) and ordered a BMP (sr-t0031).\n\nIn every renewal the old prescription was replaced by the new one. One small gap: when I closed Lena Park's lisinopril message (task-00016), I didn't link my reply to her (comm-t0015), though the reply was sent.",
